description:
Found by the sp-f1yk retroactive review (commit 44bce136). replay_objective.py's arming_verdict() computes baseline_cph against baseline=(cap=2, PROFIT), labeled 'today's live prod default' (~line 412) — but the ACTUALLY-deployed launch-path default is (cap=2, RATE) via sp-1wp8's TOUR_SOLVER_OBJECTIVE env override in main.go/run.sh. The solver's in-code fail-safe is 'profit', but prod runs 'rate'. The correct rate baseline (baseline_cap_rate_cph, line 287, returned line 300) IS computed but NEVER printed in the --arm console block (419-432), never explained in the docstring/legend, never asserted in test_arming_verdict_win. sp-ljh5 (rate arming, W3) is gated on this tool's console showing 'a clear fleet-$/hr win vs the cap-2 baseline' — but an operator reading --arm output cannot see the cph at the config the routing-service ACTUALLY runs today, so the arming decision could be made against a false (profit) baseline and arm the epic on an inflated 'win'. defaultSafetyOk=true (verification-only tool, opt-in --arm), no runtime effect — but this MUST land before sp-ljh5 trusts the gate.

FIX (from the review):
(a) print baseline_cap_rate_cph in the --arm console block alongside objective_delta_pct, explicitly labeled as the true live-prod cph (cap=2, RATE per sp-1wp8's launch default);
(b) correct the '~line 412 today's live prod default' comment to distinguish the solver's in-code fail-safe ('profit') from the launch-path env-var default ('rate');
(c) add a direct assertion on baseline_cap_rate_cph to test_arming_verdict_win, pinning against the existing _win_cases fixture (expected 1100.0).

Files: gobot/services/routing-service/replay_objective.py + tests/test_replay_objective.py. Verification-only; do NOT touch the production solve path. Depends on sp-f1yk (merged). Blocks sp-ljh5.

